@* HelpAuditPage: help topic "Audit trail" at "/help/audit-trail". Static text and screenshots. *@
@page "/help/audit-trail"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="audit-trail">
    <section class="card">
        <p>Every action is recorded in a tamper-evident chain: each entry includes a fingerprint of the one before it,
            so a changed or removed entry in the middle is detected. Anyone signed in can read the history of a
            review from its <strong>History</strong> page, and administrators of a project can read everything
            recorded for that project from the <strong>Audit trail</strong> button of its project page. System
            administrators can verify the whole chain on the <strong>Audit</strong> page. In a review with several
            reviewers that is not concluded, the entries of other people's checklist answers and of discussions about a
            check show a neutral sentence instead of the details until you hand in a ballot of your own; who acted and
            when stays visible, and your own entries always show. The lead of the review, administrators and Auditors
            see the details at once, and so does everyone in a review with a single reviewer slot or a concluded
            review.</p>
        <figure class="help-figure">
            <img class="help-shot" src="/help/audit-trail-1.png" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Audit page with the Verify chain button and a table of recorded actions with time, actor, action and detail." />
            <figcaption>The Audit page (administrators).</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
